<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gorgippia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gorgippia was an ancient Greek city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Kerch Strait</a>, on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anapa">Anapa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It developed from an earlier port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindi">Sindi</a> and was renamed after Gorgippus, a member of the ruling Spartocid family, in the fourth century BCE. A city of the Bosporan Kingdom, it prospered from the grain trade into the Roman period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gorgippia.jpg" alt="Gorgippia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This photography was created by Artem Topchiy (user Art-top). Other photos see here This photograph was taken with a ... · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anapa._Beach.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
